# Generated JSON Schemas for ctxloom JSON output (vexed-cloak); produced by
# `just gen-schemas` (build dep + CI step), like generated protobuf.
resources/schema/gen/

# Agent surface materialized by ctxloom; regenerated, never authored here.
.agents/

# Generated living-docs journey pages (like generated protobuf/JSON Schema):
# produced by `just gen-living-docs` from a passing acceptance run's capture,
# so they cannot be stale by construction. The docs CI workflow generates
# them fresh before `npm run build`; see .github/workflows/docs.yml.
website/src/content/docs/journeys/

# Serena's per-project state. Only the LOCAL and rebuildable parts are ignored;
# .serena/project.yml and .serena/memories/ are VERSIONED deliberately.
#
# Serena ships its own .serena/.gitignore excluding exactly the machine-local
# parts (/cache, /project.local.yml), which is the tool telling us the rest is
# meant to be committed. Versioning it is also what makes settings and memories
# available across git worktrees, where each worktree activates itself.
#
# Ignoring the whole directory cost us once already: project.yml drifted against
# a schema key rename, serena died at startup with a KeyError, and its symbol
# tools were silently absent from sessions rather than failing loudly. An
# unversioned config cannot drift visibly.
.serena/cache/
.serena/project.local.yml

# Working decisions log — for human review during a work session, not part of
# the repo record. FINDINGS.md and docs/behaviour-changes-*.md are the committed
# artifacts; this is the scratch ledger behind them.
DECISIONS.md

# Coverage-instrumented ctxloom (just build-cover). Same name as the shipped
# binary on purpose — see cmd/ctxloom/justfile — so it needs its own directory.
.coverbin/
